[{:db/id "q-169099/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer/id #uuid "054a9e46-29f6-5e90-a9fc-37fdcedfa68e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-169099/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "501e9194-65b8-5a25-b0b4-5cc1454659c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-169099/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd" :answer-field/choices ["q-169099/field-1/f345fac9a81ccd096b9959c6e7a966a446e93e73b82d111a376f9064132509fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-169099" :question/id #uuid "a67886c7-3468-53c0-8e99-d5012cd7aa19" :question/math-academy-id "q-169099" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The mass $M$ of a plate that occupies the region \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nwith mass density $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nM={∬}_{D}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}({3}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}9{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}9{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =[3{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =3({2}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the plate is $M=24.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-169099/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "65ae2b65-4d0c-5a25-89f8-e186eda19d33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-169099"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-169103/field-1/eaa0ff3d0e34bf4cc56606f08b4c540c17a85ab3f394397b4f1f6fe3c6d48656" :answer/id #uuid "258a3696-258b-5d2f-a938-42023bc41cf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "108" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-169103/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6936aee2-b8e0-582d-b66f-46ecbcdcfa34" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-169103/field-1/eaa0ff3d0e34bf4cc56606f08b4c540c17a85ab3f394397b4f1f6fe3c6d48656" :answer-field/choices ["q-169103/field-1/eaa0ff3d0e34bf4cc56606f08b4c540c17a85ab3f394397b4f1f6fe3c6d48656"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-169103" :question/id #uuid "1e023f2f-b319-564d-9640-5be462a7ef32" :question/math-academy-id "q-169103" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the coordinates of the center of mass of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3}{2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{y}$ of this plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\cdot 2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{y}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{y}^{2}(\\frac{81}{4}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{81}{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{27}{2}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}({2}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =108.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-169103/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fdc1a2a-8a35-59f2-9890-5b835693df4f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-169103"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-169106/field-1/cf9efe7978badeeb75cec0f3b0d2a2048a550726d402694007a38b77c125d16d" :answer/id #uuid "0a175b1b-f925-52fc-9c3e-f5b13801e3a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{228}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-169106/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a678a892-284e-55f3-8a93-e102e92f7879" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-169106/field-1/cf9efe7978badeeb75cec0f3b0d2a2048a550726d402694007a38b77c125d16d" :answer-field/choices ["q-169106/field-1/cf9efe7978badeeb75cec0f3b0d2a2048a550726d402694007a38b77c125d16d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-169106" :question/id #uuid "57467d77-fa11-5bcb-be20-65668a4ceac9" :question/math-academy-id "q-169106" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the coordinates of the center of mass of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3}{2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{y}$ of this plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $108$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nFind the radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${R}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\n\nEarlier part 7:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{s}$ of the plate about the line $s$ with equation $y=2.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{s}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{48}{5}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe moment of inertia of the plate about the axis perpendicular to the plate passing through its center of mass is ${I}_{M}=\\frac{78}{5}.$ Find the moment of inertia ${I}_{l}$ of the plate about the axis $l$ that is perpendicular to the plate and passes through the point $(1,1).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{l}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nIn part 1, we found that the mass of the plate is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe squared distance between the line through the center of mass $(2,\\frac{3}{2})$ and the line through the point $(1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}^{2} & ={(2-1)}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{2}-1)}^{2} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =\\frac{78}{5}+\\frac{5}{4}\\cdot 24 \\\\  & =\\frac{78}{5}+30 \\\\  & =\\frac{228}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-169106/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "35de55bc-23b5-574c-9fab-33c4bca720fe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-169106"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-169100/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "d183984c-4316-5da1-889c-062e0100ea7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-169100/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "50101599-38b0-5952-aec2-aaa66db8bcaa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-169100/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer-field/choices ["q-169100/field-1/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-169100" :question/id #uuid "46a2b42c-7958-5741-b473-35d19b9b5085" :question/math-academy-id "q-169100" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}$ and the plate occupies the region\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}{[{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}({3}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}9{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(2)^{4}-0 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-169100/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-169100"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-169101/field-1/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer/id #uuid "8e3cd16f-90e0-5dae-878e-6974e35fbde3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-169101/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b82cc82-b465-5e21-b729-1e7d9b51c844" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-169101/field-1/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer-field/choices ["q-169101/field-1/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-169101" :question/id #uuid "7f69c099-a398-5078-893a-c5e618c4ae16" :question/math-academy-id "q-169101" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}$ and the plate occupies the region\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{x}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{x}^{2}(\\frac{8}{3}-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{16{x}^{3}}{9}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16(3)^{3}}{9}-0 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-169101/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-169101"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-169102/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "255dfde8-adfa-5aaa-807d-05d2819a1b54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-169102/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "942c8cf7-2fe0-522e-8d35-64ef961c3aff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-169102/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-169102/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-169102/field-2/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "dc047ca6-1cf9-5fe2-bbc4-b295071a6156" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-169102/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5260cad1-40e5-54d9-beb3-2f6150d7962a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-169102/field-2/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-169102/field-2/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-169102" :question/id #uuid "f09d23db-1982-5ecb-a0dc-09360906a070" :question/math-academy-id "q-169102" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the coordinates of the center of mass of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{M},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{M}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n* $M={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n* ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n* ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nIn part 1, we found that the mass of the plate is\n\n$$\nM=24.\n$$\n\nAlso, from parts 2 and 3, we know that \n\n$$\n{M}_{x}=36,\\,{M}_{y}=48.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{M}=\\frac{48}{24}=2,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{M}=\\frac{36}{24}=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of mass of the lamina is $(2,\\frac{3}{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-169102/field-1" "q-169102/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-169102"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-169105/field-1/50243d316b735d61d679270c33ea77f72d6a9ef86b866ca12822bc02b079c957" :answer/id #uuid "b122c958-e497-565e-a75d-39b1575adf0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{48}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-169105/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a63e90b3-4ec6-5c39-9e52-691aa4b08d81" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-169105/field-1/50243d316b735d61d679270c33ea77f72d6a9ef86b866ca12822bc02b079c957" :answer-field/choices ["q-169105/field-1/50243d316b735d61d679270c33ea77f72d6a9ef86b866ca12822bc02b079c957"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-169105" :question/id #uuid "74287132-cb11-5147-aba0-d23857f5093c" :question/math-academy-id "q-169105" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the coordinates of the center of mass of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3}{2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{y}$ of this plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $108$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nFind the radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${R}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{s}$ of the plate about the line $s$ with equation $y=2.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{s}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $s$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{s}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point $(x,y)$ on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{s} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}(y-2)^{2}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4)({3}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{4}-4{y}^{3}+4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{[\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}-{y}^{4}+\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =9[\\frac{32}{5}-16+\\frac{32}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-169105/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83edde2a-daa5-50ce-b48c-3ded50a1a179"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-169105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-169104/field-1/c0604a86cfd857bc489253f78a41d2e71ce7c6f6c7bd728e03e271ea75d6c980" :answer/id #uuid "489a1c93-119b-5031-b91c-a6b9388757f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-169104/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "79edd03d-8375-560e-bf1e-01b7e48ca74b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-169104/field-1/c0604a86cfd857bc489253f78a41d2e71ce7c6f6c7bd728e03e271ea75d6c980" :answer-field/choices ["q-169104/field-1/c0604a86cfd857bc489253f78a41d2e71ce7c6f6c7bd728e03e271ea75d6c980"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-169104" :question/id #uuid "7a9f13bc-b6d0-5da3-8093-fffd0bea91d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-169104" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the coordinates of the center of mass of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3}{2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{y}$ of this plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $108$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${R}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ the radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\nIn part 1, we found that the mass of the plate is\n\n$$\nM=24.\n$$\n\nAlso, from part 5, we know that the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis is \n\n$$\n{I}_{y}=108.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{108}{24}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-169104/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bfe2e3e-9d7b-5c53-8de8-2717237d3e9c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-169104"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
